{"name":"Alfajor Brown","hex":"#a55232","fetched":"2026-10-20","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"alfajor","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A popular confection in South America usually made of flour, honey, and nuts and filled with a milk-based filling. Traditionally the filling was manjar blanco, but today it is typically dulce de leche."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alfajor"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alfajor","blocks":[{"text":"An alfajor or alajú is a traditional confection. Originally from present-day Spain, it is found now in Argentina, Bolivia, Southern Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Dominican Republic, Ecuador, El Salvador, Southern France, Paraguay, Peru, the Philippines, Uruguay, and Venezuela."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/AlfajoresP1115215_02.jpg/330px-AlfajoresP1115215_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfajor","wikidata":"Q938682"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown","wikidata":"Q47071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/AlfajoresP1115215_02.jpg/500px-AlfajoresP1115215_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn